    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d250">

                <pb facs="0297" n="273" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg273"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Harvey.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 155.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-12-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 2, 1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi>Your despatch, No. 298, dated October 23, in
                    relation to the suspicious steamer Laurel, has been received.</p>
                <p>It will be proper for you to announce to the Portuguese government that her
                    waters have been used for the equipment of another pirate to commit depredations
                    upon the commerce of the United States, and that this is the result of a
                    toleration on the part of Portugal, which is practically, though not
                    intentionally, hostile to this government, which must be expected hereafter to
                    act as its own safety shall require.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">James E. Harvey</hi>, Esq., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.,
                            &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.<hi rendition="#italic">,
                            Lisbon.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
